# Git Push on Complete

## Objective

Ship finished work to git when the **user explicitly requests** commit and/or push — not automatically after every agent change.

## When this applies

- User says commit, push, commit-and-push, or equivalent (including a commit-and-push UI action)
- **Not** after pure Q&A, reviews without code, or when the user says no commit/no push

## Conflict resolution (this repo)

`vibecoding-cost-efficient.mdc` wins: **Never commit unless the user explicitly asks.**
This file does **not** authorize silent commit/push at end of an implementation.

## Workflow (when the user asked)

1. Check `git status` / `git diff`; exclude secrets and build artifacts (`bin/`, `obj/`)
2. Stage only relevant files
3. Commit with a short why-focused message (repo style)
4. Push only if the user also asked to push (or the same commit-and-push action)
5. Report branch, message, and push result

## Git Safety

- Never change `git config`
- No `--force` on `main`/`master`
- No skipping hooks (`--no-verify`)
- No force-push / hard reset unless the user explicitly requests it

## Golden Rule

Uncommitted local work is fine until the user asks to publish it.
